DESCRIPTION:As a girl growing up in the 90s\, everyone seemed to know Rebe
 cca had Autism Spectrum Disorder except for her! And her parents! However\
 , one thing was crystal clear: she had no idea how to “act normal.” Th
 is show will cover Rebecca's hilarious journey of self-exploration and her
  lifelong struggle to adapt\, including at one point literally googling 
 “how to act normal” and landing on the pinnacle of the ‘00s internet
 : WikiHow.\nABOUT REBECCA\nRebecca Kaplan is an adorably awkward standup c
 omedian. Her acerbic wit and relatable insights have entertained crowds al
 l over the world. She's appeared on the Late Show with David Letterman and
  has been featured on SiriusXM\, NPR\, and the front page of WorldStarHipH
 op. She lives in NYC\, where she co-hosts the Bad Fan Fic podcast. Follow 
 her on all social media at @RebeccaTKaplan to check out her clips.\n\n$15\
 , 21+\n\nTickets: https://consumer.pxf.io/APvP5J?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.event
 brite.com%2Fe%2Frebecca-kaplan-how-to-act-normal-at-mr-bings-sf-tickets-19
 99318920712\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/16/rebecca-kapla
 n-how-to-act-normal-comedy-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
